{"id":"bb38790ef6a3828c","group":"92","path":"92/92-df-recursion-closed.md","title":"Recursive Function Closure","display":"df-recursion-closed — Recursive Function Closure","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems","book_abbrev":"92","label":"92-df-recursion-closed","aliases":["92-df-recursion-closed"],"display":"df-recursion-closed — Recursive Function Closure","depends_on":["[[92-df-recursive-function]]","[[92-df-composition]]","[[92-df-recursion-operator]]","[[92-df-unbounded-minimization]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"92"},{"key":"label","html":"92-df-recursion-closed"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>92-df-recursion-closed</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-recursion-closed — Recursive Function Closure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d65795dc15ebce4b\" href=\"?note=d65795dc15ebce4b\" title=\"92-df-recursive-function\">92-df-recursive-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7d55d92fc12a07fc\" href=\"?note=7d55d92fc12a07fc\" title=\"92-df-composition\">92-df-composition</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8940b60e44b8fbd8\" href=\"?note=8940b60e44b8fbd8\" title=\"92-df-recursion-operator\">92-df-recursion-operator</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"3f3056569f28b91e\" href=\"?note=3f3056569f28b91e\" title=\"92-df-unbounded-minimization\">92-df-unbounded-minimization</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C\\subseteq\\mathsf{PF}\">\\(C\\subseteq\\mathsf{PF}\\)</span> (candidate partial-function class)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{PF},\\mathrm{PartRec}\">\\(\\mathsf{PF},\\mathrm{PartRec}\\)</span> (partial-function universe and partial-recursive class, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d65795dc15ebce4b\" href=\"?note=d65795dc15ebce4b\" title=\"92-df-recursive-function\">92-df-recursive-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Comp}_{k,m}\">\\(\\mathrm{Comp}_{k,m}\\)</span> (composition operator, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"7d55d92fc12a07fc\" href=\"?note=7d55d92fc12a07fc\" title=\"92-df-composition\">92-df-composition</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RecOp}_k\">\\(\\mathrm{RecOp}_k\\)</span> (recursion operator, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"8940b60e44b8fbd8\" href=\"?note=8940b60e44b8fbd8\" title=\"92-df-recursion-operator\">92-df-recursion-operator</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu_k\">\\(\\mu_k\\)</span> (minimization operator, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"3f3056569f28b91e\" href=\"?note=3f3056569f28b91e\" title=\"92-df-unbounded-minimization\">92-df-unbounded-minimization</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RecClosed}\">\\(\\mathrm{RecClosed}\\)</span> (definition-target predicate)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}recursion\\text{-}closed} \\vdash \\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{RecClosed}(C)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;C\\subseteq\\mathsf{PF}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\,\\forall m\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\,\n\\forall g\\in C\\cap(\\mathbb N^m\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\,\n\\forall(h_1,\\ldots,h_m)\\in\\bigl(C\\cap(\\mathbb N^k\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\bigr)^m\\;\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Comp}_{k,m}(g,h_1,\\ldots,h_m)\\in C\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\,\n\\forall g\\in C\\cap(\\mathbb N^k\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\,\n\\forall h\\in C\\cap(\\mathbb N^{k+2}\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\;\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{RecOp}_k(g,h)\\in C\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\,\n\\forall g\\in C\\cap(\\mathbb N^{k+1}\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\;\n\\bigl(\\mu_k(g)\\in C\\bigr),\\\\\n&amp;\\mathrm{RecClosed}(\\mathrm{PartRec}).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}recursion\\text{-}closed} \\vdash \\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{RecClosed}(C)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;C\\subseteq\\mathsf{PF}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\,\\forall m\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\,\n\\forall g\\in C\\cap(\\mathbb N^m\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\,\n\\forall(h_1,\\ldots,h_m)\\in\\bigl(C\\cap(\\mathbb N^k\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\bigr)^m\\;\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Comp}_{k,m}(g,h_1,\\ldots,h_m)\\in C\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\,\n\\forall g\\in C\\cap(\\mathbb N^k\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\,\n\\forall h\\in C\\cap(\\mathbb N^{k+2}\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\;\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{RecOp}_k(g,h)\\in C\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\,\n\\forall g\\in C\\cap(\\mathbb N^{k+1}\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N)\\;\n\\bigl(\\mu_k(g)\\in C\\bigr),\\\\\n&amp;\\mathrm{RecClosed}(\\mathrm{PartRec}).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>关键符号：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>部分递归函数类的封闭性</li>\n<li>封闭于复合</li>\n<li>封闭于原始递归</li>\n<li>封闭于无界极小化</li>\n<li>总递归函数类不对任意无界极小化封闭；闭包断言属于 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartRec}\">\\(\\mathrm{PartRec}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartRec}\">\\(\\mathrm{PartRec}\\)</span> 是包含 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PR}\">\\(\\mathrm{PR}\\)</span> 且对三类部分函数算子封闭的最小类</li>\n<li>与固定 Turing 机模型的等价性是另一个可证明的模型等价定理</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"92-df-recursive-function",